  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-9 End
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: At Barcelona, I met many people that were my schoolmates in Ateneo,
      some even recognized me by name. We held reunions every other Sunday at the
      cafe as we could not do it the same way as the Spanish do with our limited
      resources
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 3
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I remained in Barcelona for a short time, long enough, to see the historic
      sights in the city. Which was established by Hannibal, numbered many noted
      Romans among its residents, and in later days was the scene of the return of
      Columbus from his voyages in the New World, bringing with him samples of Redskins,
      birds and other novel products of the unknown country.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "Then there were the magnificent boulevards, the handsome dwellings,
      the interest which the citizens took in adorning their city and the pride in
      the results, and above all, the disgust at all things Spanish and the loyalty
      to Catalonia, rather than to the \u201Cmother-fatherland."
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: All these things impressed me when I had seen in my own country the
      most respectfully worded complaints of unquestionable abuses treated as treason,
      bringing not merely punishment, but opprobrium as well.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: In order to obtain better education, I had to leave my country stealthily
      like a fugitive from justice, and my family, to save themselves from persecution,
      were compelled to profess ignorance of his plans and movements.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Early fall, I went to Madrid and entered Central University there.
      I went to Barcelona to correct my passport, as it would be easier to obtain
      a cedula so that my time in the university would be smoother. I enrolled in
      two courses, medicine, literature, and philosophy. I studied sculpture, drawing
      and art in San Carlos, and took private lessons in languages from a well-known
      instructor in the city called Mr. Hughes.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: With my time here in Madrid, I did not mingle in social life as I was
      occupied with my work. Some may say it's because I did not have enough money,
      but I disagree. I left Manila with 700 pesos and a diamond ring. I receive
      funds from my father, so that I can continue on with my studies. It was no
      easy task for me, who had to secretly leave to study abroad.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 2
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I indulged in entertainment from time to time. I watched high class
      theaters from time to time, I even gambled in small amounts regularly. But
      I spent most of my money to buy books. These books were bought second-hand
      but they're still in good condition. Buying these books taught me a lot. It
      expanded my perception of the world and that there are different ways people
      from different nations ruled the land.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
